1
00:00:00,277 --> 00:00:02,277
(Sheldon:)-So you betrayed me.
-No.

2
00:00:02,446 --> 00:00:03,576
(Penny:)It wasn't a betrayal.

3
00:00:03,739 --> 00:00:06,739
It was more of a, I can't afford
any more points on my license.

4
00:00:06,909 --> 00:00:10,579
(Penny:)I already have to buy my insurance
from this place in the Cayman Islands.

5
00:00:10,746 --> 00:00:12,916
(Sheldon:)But the only reason
I was driving your car...

6
00:00:13,082 --> 00:00:16,042
(Sheldon:)...was because you were in distress,
and I was rescuing you.

7
00:00:16,210 --> 00:00:19,920
Yes. And look, now you have a photo
to remember that heroic day.

8
00:00:21,465 --> 00:00:22,965
(Leonard:)It's not that big a deal.

9
00:00:23,133 --> 00:00:26,473
(Leonard:)You just go down to the court on Thursday,
and you pay the fine.

10
00:00:26,637 --> 00:00:29,727
(Sheldon:)I'm not going to pay a fine.
That would imply I'm guilty.

11
00:00:29,890 --> 00:00:31,270
(Howard:)You are guilty.

12
00:00:32,810 --> 00:00:34,770
[LAW & ORDER'S "THE CLANG"
PLAYS OVER SPEAKER]

13
00:00:37,689 --> 00:00:40,149
(Howard:)-That one I liked.
-Yeah.

14
00:00:40,818 --> 00:00:43,148
(Sheldon:)I am not guilty.
I only have a learner's permit.

15
00:00:43,320 --> 00:00:45,780
(Sheldon:)Penny was the teacher.
When the light turned yellow...

16
00:00:45,948 --> 00:00:48,868
...she said, "Go, go, go,"
so I went, went, went.

17
00:00:49,076 --> 00:00:52,366
(Penny:)Sheldon, I'm sorry. I'll be happy
to reimburse you for the fine.

18
00:00:52,579 --> 00:00:56,289
(Penny:)You know, as soon as I get a part
in a movie or my own TV series.

19
00:00:56,458 --> 00:00:58,668
(Sheldon:)You don't need to reimburse me.
I'm not paying.

20
00:00:58,836 --> 00:01:02,796
(Sheldon:)On Thursday, I will have my day in court,
and justice will be done.

